# Build the demo database

Request: $ARGUMENTS

1. Run `uv run {{ project_name }} demo` with the parameters the user gave (`--seed`, `--days`; see
   `uv run {{ project_name }} demo --help`). It writes `data/demo.duckdb`. It replaces an earlier demo database only,
   never the real one or any other file.
2. Report what it wrote: the days and the seed.
3. To show it, start the app on it: `/app start demo` (`{{ project_name }} app --demo`).

The demo database holds a `demo_params` table: the parameters it was built from. `publish` refuses a database
that holds it, so made-up data never goes where the real data goes.

This skill is the app's own (the scaffold writes it once): describe here the parameters of this app's generator
(`src/{{ package }}/demo.py`), and what to ask the user before a build.
